cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the corpus it collected, cite the 2021 article
  below (preferred-citation) and this archived release. The code is a
  modification of Bernardo Pires's twitch-chat-logger (see references).
type: software
title: dissertation_logger
abstract: >-
  Twitch chat and stream-metadata logger used to collect the corpus behind
  Leith (2021), Communication Monographs. Archived as it ran in December 2018
  and January 2019. It targets the retired Twitch API v5 (Kraken) and does not
  run against the current Twitch API; version 2 is a planned port.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/apleith/dissertation_logger"
keywords:
  - Twitch
  - livestreaming
  - chat logs
  - IRC
  - PostgreSQL
  - parasocial relationships
authors:
  - family-names: Leith
    given-names: Alex P.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1310-6763"
    affiliation: Southern Illinois University Edwardsville
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Parasocial cues: The ubiquity of parasocial relationships on Twitch"
  authors:
    - family-names: Leith
      given-names: Alex P.
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1310-6763"
  journal: Communication Monographs
  volume: 88
  issue: 1
  start: 111
  end: 129
  year: 2021
  doi: 10.1080/03637751.2020.1868544
references:
  - type: software
    title: twitch-chat-logger
    authors:
      - family-names: Pires
        given-names: Bernardo
    year: 2015
    license: MIT
    repository-code: "https://github.com/bernardopires/twitch-chat-logger"
    notes: >-
      The original work. dissertation_logger keeps its architecture and most of
      its code; the changes are the per-category stream filter, the partner and
      language filters, timing constants, and the database schema names.
